     "Governor",
     "Chief Minister",
     "Legislative Assembly",
     "State List",
     "High Court",
     "Council of Ministers"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Each state has a legislature, an executive and a judiciary. The Governor is the head of state, appointed by the President. The Chief Minister is the head of government and leads the Council of Ministers responsible to the Legislative Assembly.\nThe Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) is elected by people for five years. Some states, like Tamil Nadu earlier, had a Legislative Council. The Assembly makes laws on State List subjects such as police, public health and agriculture.\nThe High Court is the highest court of the state, and the Madras High Court serves Tamil Nadu. Local bodies and the state work together."
    }
